605 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 318 0 R
/E (Across this age band, the central distinction is whether AI strengthens caregiver responsiveness or replaces elements of it. The same feature, such as monitoring or responsiveness, can support development when it helps a caregiver notice and respond, but create risk when the system itself becomes the source of stimulation or simulated interaction. The policy signal is that interaction design and use context matter more than content alone: infant-directed systems that mediate or simulate core relational processes should be treated differently from caregiver-support tools.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
