608 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 2117 0 R
/E (Caregiver support: May provide short periods of engagement or soothing in constrained situations, especially during co-use with caregivers, especially when visual access to screens is not involved. Benefits to the child are likely indirect, situational, and derived from support of caregiver functions, rather than developmental.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
609 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 2118 0 R
/E (Simulated social contingency and socioemotional disruptions: Systems that mimic responsiveness may interfere with attachment-related processes and expose infants to simulated social contingency without the social/relational inputs development requires, producing the form of attachment without the function. Systems that are too engaging or that involve screens may increase physiological arousal and disrupt soothing and sleep. )
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
