/P 2289 0 R
/E (Poor epistemic practices: Some systems encourage students to write first and attach evidence afterward or to make AI-generated text sound more human, in ways that obscure authorship. This confuses academic writing as a learning process with the mere production of a finished output. Over time, such tools may normalize misrepresentation, weaken source-based reasoning, and undermine epistemic judgment.)
/Pg 38 0 R
/K [10]
>>
